<title>USA: Medcross yr shr loss $6.53 after I-Link buy.</title>
<headline>Medcross yr shr loss $6.53 after I-Link buy.</headline>
<dateline>SALT LAKE CITY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medcross Inc.</p>
<p>			 Selected Financial Data</p>
<p>							 1996	  1995</p>
<p> Net Operating Revenue		    $2,383,076  $3,122,953</p>
<p> Operating Loss			   (20,192,514)   (493,755)</p>
<p> Total Other Expense		     (2,876,626)    (70,594)</p>
<p> Net Loss				   (23,064,240)   (551,909)</p>
<p>Net Loss per Common Share after</p>
<p>  Preferred Dividends			   (6.53)	(0.39)</p>
<p>			   Medcross, Inc.</p>
<p>	     Selected Balance Sheet Information</p>
<p>					     1996	    1995</p>
<p> Total Current Assets	  $6,105,553     $1,918,350</p>
<p> Total Assets		    11,433,830	4,146,863</p>
<p> Total Stockholders' Equity   6,298,617	1,455,166</p>
<p>Total Liabilities and</p>
<p>  Stockholders Equity	  11,433,830	4,146,863</p>
<p>The company attributed its net loss in 1996 primarily to a non-cash expense of $14,577,942 of acquired in-process research and development costs related to acquisition of I-Link Worldwide Inc in February 1996.</p>
<p>The company said the acquisition of I-Link Worldwide Inc was accounted for under the purchase method of accounting.</p>
